      "content": "The inclusion of zero in the 95% confidence interval is often a strong indicator that the result is not robust, even if the p-value is just below the threshold. You can explain this tension by framing it as a discrepancy between statistical significance and practical significance. Argue that while the data *suggests* a relationship, the wide CI implies the effect size is relatively small and highly uncertain, thus limiting the practical weight of the finding in your discussion. This balanced approach demonstrates sophisticated statistical literacy.",
