      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Essentially, the conflict is often rooted in a combination of sample size and variability (noise). A smaller sample size generally leads to wider, less precise confidence intervals, even with a highly significant p-value. Conversely, very high variance in the data can inflate the CI width, even if the point estimate yields a low p-value. The p-value tests the null hypothesis generally, while the CI quantifies the plausible range of the true effect.",
